* TOOL_REMOTE
* Everything that lets a machine or a person reach SD from outside, on one screen: the two doors (the API and ssh) as the machine reports them, how each account can be reached, the SDNet
* servers, who is connected now, and this machine's TLS identity (S.75, plan .claude/plan-fullscreen-toolkit.md section 5, A9).
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 12 Nov 26 Windows port - RELEASE_1.1 243: the status line says "Reading the setting" while the two reports run (as SD Core Solo), and the verbs' own
*           wait line is taken off the captured report.
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux (S.75 A9, df48c780, and its later changes to S.186 ad4a2cf6; RELEASE_1.1 228), agreed with Linux by mail 2026-11-11T0630.  Five views,
*               not six: the sdsys login view (REMOTE.SDSYS, S.95 and S.106) is left out, as remote administration over ssh is deferred here (RELEASE_1.1 202), so 6, O and F
*               and the verb are gone.  OS deviations: A hands the terminal to REMOTE.API instead of running it through $tk_run, because the Windows verb asks whether to
*               restart SD when the listener moves to or from OFF (the socket is opened only at start-up, and a restart ends every session); the doors' words are what
*               api-listener.ps1, api-firewall.ps1 and ssh-firewall.ps1 read back from sd.conf and the firewall rules; a route is a Windows group; "Press Enter" is 12870.
* 02 Nov 26 dm  S.106: the authenticator code is removed (owner: password only for this release).  The sdsys login view reports whether sshd lets sdsys in; O opens it (REMOTE.SDSYS ON,
*               after a box wanting the word OPEN) and F shuts it (OFF); R (recovery codes) and L (the code at the console) are gone.
* 02 Nov 26 dm  S.101 stage D: L on the sdsys login view - REMOTE.SDSYS LOCAL ON or OFF after a box (the code at the console too, or not; off as delivered).
* 28 Oct 26 dm  S.88 L2: the three boxes are panes of the layout service ($tk_layout): drawn exactly as before at 140 by 43, and in a larger window the list takes the extra rows, every
*               box and text is as wide as the window, and the explanation wraps at the box's width. The rows, widths, hit tests and the [?] button are counted from the pane rectangles.
*               The layout is declared again after the terminal was given to SET.SERVER and the screen taken again.
* 25 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line ($tk_aipage), as tool.voc has it: F6 or AI > Ask the AI; the five views and refresh are offered, nothing that opens a door.
* 1 Nov 26 dm  S.95 stage 1b: a sixth view, the sdsys login over ssh: REMOTE.SDSYS's report, and O, R and F give the terminal to REMOTE.SDSYS ON, RECOVERY and OFF after a box
*              (the secret and the recovery codes are shown by the verb on the plain terminal and never pass through this page).
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 are the box keys of every page ($tk_aipage 'ring'): from the view to the AI line and back; AI > Ask the AI is a menu entry of its own.
* 8 Nov 26 dm  S.179: Ctrl-T the theme (View > Theme) and Ctrl-K the keys of the page (Help > Keys), through $tk_std as on every page.
* 9 Nov 26 dm  S.186: View > Mouse and Ctrl-O (the log of the commands run), the same on every page (the cases act:std.mouse and ctrl-o, through $tk_std).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   TOOL.REMOTE      (SDSYS's VOC only; the audience is the administrator, asked of the kernel before anything is read)
*
*   A full-screen page, in the toolkit's frame (140 columns by 43 lines at least), of five views, chosen with the keys 1 to 5:
*     1  the doors     REMOTE.API and REMOTE.SSH with no keyword, which report what the machine says (sd.conf's APIPORT and the firewall rules read back, not an intention): the list
*                      is their words.  A changes the API (ON, LOCAL or OFF): after its box the terminal is given to REMOTE.API, which asks whether to restart SD when the listener
*                      moves to or from OFF.  S changes ssh (ON or OFF) through the routine.  ON lets other computers in, so either box wants the word OPEN typed.
*     2  routes        every USER account with the doors it has (ssh, api, files, files-write, files-admin) and the NET gate, and in words how that account can be reached.  It only
*                      shows: the switches are TOOL.GATES's.
*     3  servers       the SDNet servers of the servers file (!netdefs): name, host:port, the remote account and the mode, the pin shortened, the local accounts that may use it.  X deletes
*                      the one under the cursor (DELETE.SERVER, after a box).  N defines one: the fields are asked and checked here, and the terminal is given to SET.SERVER, whose
*                      CONNECT step shows the key the server presents and asks whether to trust it.
*     4  connected     every session now, by the door it came through: the user number, the kind (user, api, sdnet, phantom), the login user, the account and where it came from.
*     5  TLS           this machine's own TLS identity as SETTINGS.REPORT gives it: the certificate fields and the public-key hash another SD server pins.  Never the private key.
*   Keys: Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn, Home, End; F5 reads again; F1 or ? or a click on the [?] explains the page; Ctrl-Q leaves.  A click on a row puts the cursor there.
*
*   WHAT IT RUNS.  Each change only after its box was answered Run (Cancel is what Enter chooses): REMOTE.API and REMOTE.SSH with no keyword through the routine (to report);
*   REMOTE.SSH ON or OFF and DELETE.SERVER through the routine; REMOTE.API ON, LOCAL or OFF and SET.SERVER on the terminal, given to the verb.  LIST.SERVERS is not run (the file
*   is read with !netdefs).  The verbs ask for the administrator again and write their own audit lines.  The page writes nothing itself.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program $tool_remote
$catalog $tool_remote

$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h
$include err.h
$include sl.h
$include tk.h

   prompt ''

   allow = 'remote.api remote.ssh delete.server'   ;* the commands this page may run through the routine (remote.api only to report; a change of it and set.server go to the verb on the terminal)
   call $tk_open('tool.remote', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      stop
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, 'tool start app=tool.remote')

   keys = ''
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f1', 'help', 'help', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '1', 'doors', 'doors', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '2', 'routes', 'routes', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '3', 'servers', 'servers', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '4', 'connected', 'connected', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, '5', 'tls', 'tls', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'a', 'api', 'api', 'Doors', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 's', 'ssh', 'ssh', 'Doors', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'x', 'delete', 'delete', 'Servers', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'n', 'new', 'new', 'Servers', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'f5', 'read', 'refresh', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'ctrl-q', 'quit', 'quit', '', 1)
   call $tk_keys('add', keys, 'esc', 'menu', 'menu', '', 1)                ;* S.88 U4: Esc goes back to the doors view first, else opens the menu bar
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'quit', '&File', '&Quit', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'api', '&Door', '&API door on or off', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'ssh', '&Door', '&Ssh door on or off', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'delete', '&Server', '&Delete the server', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'new', '&Server', '&New server', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'doors', '&View', '&Doors', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'routes', '&View', '&Routes', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'servers', '&View', '&Servers', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'connected', '&View', '&Connected', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'tls', '&View', '&TLS', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'refresh', '&View', 'Re&fresh', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('menu', keys, 'help', '&Help', '&Help on this page', '', '')
   call $tk_std('keys', ctx, keys, '', '')                ;* S.179: Ctrl-T theme, Ctrl-K keys and their View and Help entries, as on every page
   panes = 'Doors' : @fm : 'Routes' : @fm : 'Servers' : @fm : 'Connected' : @fm : 'TLS'
   * S.97 stage 2 (group B): the AI line.  The page offers the AI only its five views and refresh (opening or closing ssh or the API, a new server and deleting one are
   * NOT offered without the owner's word); a proposal is carried out by the page's own key.  Where the AI is not usable nothing here adds a key, a row or a line.
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'doors', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'routes', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'servers', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'connected', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'tls', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_keys('ai', keys, 'refresh', '', '', '', '')
   call $tk_aipage('init', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)

   gosub lay.declare                                            ;* the panes; VR (the list rows on the screen) and DV (the explanation rows) come from them
   view = 1
   rowtxt = '' ; nrows = 0 ; hdr = ''
   api.out = '' ; ssh.out = ''
   defs = '' ; nsrv = 0
   udata = '' ; nsess = 0
   unames = '' ; nu = 0
   ugates = ''
   tls.lines = ''
   ci = 1 ; ta = 0
   gen = 0
   done = 0
   msg = ''

   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all

   loop
      call $tk_menubar('draw', ctx, keys, panes<view>, '', '', mr)          ;* the bar first: it writes row 0 whole, and the frame then writes the app name at its right end
      call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, panes<view>, msg)
      call $sl_curat(0, ctx<TK.C.YSTAT>)
      nm = ''
      screen key returning nm
      mr = ''
      ao = ''
      if nm # '' then call $tk_aipage('key', ctx, keys, panes<view>, nm, ao)         ;* S.97 stage 2: while the AI line has the focus it takes the keys, before the bar sees them
      if ao<1> = 'replay' then nm = ao<2>                                            ;* an action the AI proposed and the person accepted: this page's own key for it
      if ao<1> # '' then msg = ao<4>
      busy = (if view # 1 then 1 else 0)
      if nm # '' and ao<1> = '' then call $tk_menubar('key', ctx, keys, panes<view>, nm, busy, mr)       ;* the Esc rule: another view is left before the bar opens
      if mr<1> # '' then nm = mr<4>
      begin case
         case ao<1> = 'taken'
            if ao<3> then
               gen += 1                                                               ;* the preview, the wait and the answer covered the page: all of it is drawn again
               ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
               gosub draw.all
            end
         case nm = ''
            if status() = ER$EOF then exit
         case nm = 'guardquit'
            exit
         case nm = 'resize'
            call $tk_layout('refresh', ctx, '', lay.chg)
            gosub lay.get
            gen += 1
            ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
            gosub draw.all
         case nm = 'mouse'
            gosub on.mouse
         case 1
            gosub on.key
      end case
      if done then exit
   repeat

   call $tk_close(ctx)
   stop

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- what the machine says

* Everything the five views show, read again: the doors' reports, the SDNet servers, the sessions, the accounts' routes and the TLS lines
read.all:
*  12 Nov 26 (RELEASE_1.1 243): the two reports start PowerShell, a few seconds: the status line says so first (owner, 12 Nov 26, a line
*  before any wait over 2 s; SD Core Solo's tool_remote does the same), and the page's own message comes back after.
   held.msg = msg
   msg = sysmsg(12950)                                          ;* Reading the setting (a few seconds)...
   call $tk_frame(ctx, keys, panes<view>, msg)
   msg = held.msg
   sel.t = ''
   if nrows > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nrows then sel.t = rowtxt<ci>
   cmd = 'remote.api'
   gosub run.report
   api.out = rep
   cmd = 'remote.ssh'
   gosub run.report
   ssh.out = rep
   call !netdefs('READ', defs, nderr)
   if nderr # '' then defs = ''
   nsrv = dcount(defs, @fm)
   call !listu(udata)
   nsess = dcount(udata, @fm)
   gosub read.accounts
   call !settings_os(os.lines, soerr)
   tls.lines = ''
   if soerr = '' then
      inapi = 0
      for i = 1 to dcount(os.lines, @fm)
         l = os.lines<i>
         if l[1, 1] = '[' then inapi = (l[1, 5] = '[api]')
         if inapi and l[1, 5] # '[api]' then tls.lines<-1> = l
      next i
   end
   gosub build.rows
   if sel.t # '' then
      for i = 1 to nrows
         if rowtxt<i> = sel.t then
            ci = i
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   if ci > nrows then ci = nrows
   if ci < 1 then ci = 1
   return

* cmd is a verb with no keyword (it reports and changes nothing); rep is what it printed, or why it was not run
run.report:
   call $tk_run(allow, cmd, rep, rstat, rerr)
   if rerr # '' then rep = rerr
* a message with line breaks is several rows, never one row that moves the cursor (a message writes \n as LF then CR, so the CR that is left starts the next row at column 0)
   rep = change(change(change(rep, char(13) : char(10), @fm), char(10), @fm), char(13), '')
   if trim(rep<1>) = trim(sysmsg(12950)) or trim(rep<1>) = trim(sysmsg(12944)) then del rep<1>   ;* 12 Nov 26: the verb's wait line; the status line said it
   if rstat # 0 and trim(rep) = '' then rep = cmd : ' returned status ' : rstat
   return

* The USER accounts, in name order, with the state of the doors and the NET gate
read.accounts:
   names = ''
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : 'accounts' to acc.f then
      select acc.f to 9
      loop
         readnext id from 9 else exit
         if id # 'sdsys' then
            locate id in names<1> by 'AL' setting lp else
               ins id before names<lp>
            end
         end
      repeat
      close acc.f
   end
   unames = '' ; ugates = '' ; nu = 0
   for i = 1 to dcount(names, @fm)
      call $tk_gates(names<i>, g, ainfo, gerr)
      if gerr = '' and ainfo<1> = 'USER' then
         nu += 1
         unames<nu> = names<i>
         st.s = ''
         for j = 1 to dcount(g, @fm)
            gid = g<j, 1>
            if gid = 'ssh' or gid = 'api' or gid = 'files' or gid = 'files-write' or gid = 'files-admin' or gid = 'net' then
               st.s := (if st.s = '' then '' else ' ') : gid : '=' : g<j, 2>
            end
         next j
         ugates<nu> = st.s
      end
   next i
   return

* The rows of the view that is showing, and the heading above them
build.rows:
   rowtxt = '' ; nrows = 0
   begin case
      case view = 1
         hdr = 'What the machine says (REMOTE.API, then REMOTE.SSH, with no keyword)'
         for i = 1 to dcount(api.out, @fm)
            if trim(api.out<i>) # '' then rowtxt<-1> = api.out<i>
         next i
         rowtxt<-1> = ''
         for i = 1 to dcount(ssh.out, @fm)
            if trim(ssh.out<i>) # '' then rowtxt<-1> = ssh.out<i>
         next i
      case view = 2
         hdr = fmt('Account', '20L') : fmt('ssh', '6L') : fmt('api', '6L') : fmt('files', '7L') : fmt('write', '7L') : fmt('admin', '7L') : fmt('net', '6L') : 'How it can be reached'
         for i = 1 to nu
            gosub route.line
            rowtxt<-1> = rline
         next i
      case view = 3
         hdr = fmt('Name', '17L') : fmt('Address', '34L') : fmt('Remote account / mode', '24L') : fmt('Pin', '21L') : 'Local accounts that may use it'
         for i = 1 to nsrv
            d = defs<i>
            allowed = d<1, 7>
            if allowed = '' then allowed = 'none'
            pn = d<1, 5>
            rowtxt<-1> = fmt(d<1, 1>, '17L') : fmt(d<1, 2> : ':' : d<1, 3>, '34L') : fmt(d<1, 4> : '/' : d<1, 6>, '24L') : fmt(pn[1, 16] : '...', '21L') : allowed
         next i
      case view = 4
         hdr = fmt('User', '6R') : '  ' : fmt('Kind', '9L') : fmt('Login user', '16L') : fmt('Account', '20L') : 'Came from'
         for i = 1 to nsess
            gosub session.line
            rowtxt<-1> = sline
         next i
      case 1
         hdr = 'The certificate and public-key lines of SETTINGS.REPORT [api]; the private key is never read'
         for i = 1 to dcount(tls.lines, @fm)
            if trim(tls.lines<i>) # '' then rowtxt<-1> = tls.lines<i>
         next i
   end case
   nrows = dcount(rowtxt, @fm)
   if rowtxt = '' then nrows = 0
   return

* One USER account (i is its place in unames) as a line: the doors it has and what that means
route.line:
   gs = ugates<i>
   cell.ssh = (if index(gs, 'ssh=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   cell.api = (if index(gs, 'api=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   cell.files = (if index(gs, 'files=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   cell.fw = (if index(gs, 'files-write=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   cell.fa = (if index(gs, 'files-admin=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   cell.net = (if index(gs, 'net=1', 1) then 'yes' else 'no')
   reach = ''
   if cell.api = 'yes' then reach<-1> = 'the whole API'
   if cell.api = 'no' and cell.files = 'yes' then
      w = 'files only (read)'
      if cell.fw = 'yes' then w = 'files only (read and write)'
      if cell.fa = 'yes' then w = 'files only (read, write and administer)'
      reach<-1> = w
   end
   if cell.ssh = 'yes' then reach<-1> = 'ssh'
   if reach = '' then reach = 'no remote door'
   rline = fmt(unames<i>[1, 19], '20L') : fmt(cell.ssh, '6L') : fmt(cell.api, '6L') : fmt(cell.files, '7L') : fmt(cell.fw, '7L') : fmt(cell.fa, '7L') : fmt(cell.net, '6L') : convert(@fm, ', ', reach)
   return

* One session (i is its place in udata) as a line
session.line:
   v = udata<i>
   flg = v<1, 4>
   kind = 'user'
   begin case
      case bitand(flg, USR$SDNET)
         kind = 'sdnet'
      case bitand(flg, USR$SDVBSRVR)
         kind = 'api'
      case bitand(flg, USR$PHANTOM)
         kind = 'phantom'
   end case
   org = v<1, 3>
   if v<1, 7> # '' then org := (if org = '' then '' else ' ') : v<1, 7>
   sline = fmt(v<1, 1>, '6R') : '  ' : fmt(kind, '9L') : fmt(v<1, 6>, '16L') : fmt(v<1, 9>, '20L') : org
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the layout (S.88 L2)

* The page's three boxes as panes of $tk_layout: each size is the box drawn at 140 by 43 (the body is 138 by 39), so at that size nothing moves; in a larger window the list stretches
* (a table shows more rows) and every pane is as wide as the body.  Declared again after the terminal was given away and the screen taken again.
lay.declare:
   d = ''
   d<1> = 'top' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 6 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<2> = 'list' : @vm : 2 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 20 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1 : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   d<3> = 'detail' : @vm : 3 : @vm : 1 : @vm : 13 : @vm : 138 : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : '' : @vm : 'stretch' : @vm : 1
   call $tk_layout('declare', ctx, d, lay.err)
   gosub lay.get
   return

* The rectangles of the three panes, and what is counted from them: tw the width of a text line inside a box (134 at 140 by 43), VR the list rows, DV the explanation rows
lay.get:
   lay.id = 'top'
   gosub lay.rect
   top.x = lay.x ; top.y = lay.y ; top.w = lay.w ; top.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'list'
   gosub lay.rect
   lst.x = lay.x ; lst.y = lay.y ; lst.w = lay.w ; lst.h = lay.h
   lay.id = 'detail'
   gosub lay.rect
   det.x = lay.x ; det.y = lay.y ; det.w = lay.w ; det.h = lay.h
   body.y = ctx<TK.C.YBODY>
   tx = lst.x + 2
   tw = lst.w - 4
   mk.x = top.x + top.w - 5                                     ;* the [?] button, at the right end of the first row of the top box
   mk.y = top.y + 1
   VR = lst.h - 3
   DV = det.h - 2
   return

lay.rect:
   call $tk_layout('pane', ctx, lay.id, lay.r)
   lay.x = lay.r<1, 1>
   lay.y = lay.r<1, 2>
   lay.w = lay.r<1, 3>
   lay.h = lay.r<1, 4>
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- drawing

draw.all:
   cw2 = ctx<TK.C.W>
   chh = ctx<TK.C.H> - 5
   screen clear at 0,body.y size cw2,chh
   screen box at top.x,top.y size top.w,top.h title 'Remote access'
   t.list = 'The doors'
   if view = 2 then t.list = 'The routes of the user accounts'
   if view = 3 then t.list = 'SDNet servers'
   if view = 4 then t.list = 'Connected now'
   if view = 5 then t.list = 'TLS identity of this machine'
   screen box at lst.x,lst.y size lst.w,lst.h title t.list
   screen box at det.x,det.y size det.w,det.h title 'About this view'
   gosub draw.top
   gosub redraw
   return

draw.top:
   ap = trim(api.out<1>)
   sp = trim(ssh.out<1>)
   s = 'API: ' : ap
   screen text s[1, tw - 6] at tx,top.y + 1 attr 'bold' width tw - 6                  ;* 6 less than the other lines so that the [?] is clear
   s = 'ssh: ' : sp
   screen text s[1, tw] at tx,top.y + 2 width tw
   s = nsrv : ' SDNet server' : (if nsrv = 1 then '' else 's') : ' defined.   ' : nu : ' user account' : (if nu = 1 then '' else 's') : '.   ' : nsess : ' session' : (if nsess = 1 then '' else 's') : ' now.'
   screen text s at tx,top.y + 3 width tw
   screen text '1 doors  2 routes  3 servers  4 connected  5 TLS   doors: A api, S ssh  servers: X delete, N new' at tx,top.y + 4 width tw
   call $tk_help('mark', mk.x, mk.y, 0, 0)
   return

redraw:
   gosub draw.list
   gosub draw.detail
   return

draw.list:
   screen text hdr[1, tw] at tx,lst.y + 1 attr 'header' width tw
   if ci <= ta then ta = ci - 1
   if ci > ta + VR then ta = ci - VR
   if ta < 0 then ta = 0
   for r = 1 to VR
      kk = ta + r
      s = ''
      if kk <= nrows then s = rowtxt<kk>
      rat = 'normal'
      if kk = ci and kk <= nrows and view # 1 and view # 5 then rat = 'highlight'
      screen text s[1, tw] at tx,lst.y + 1 + r attr rat width tw
   next r
   return

draw.detail:
   for r = 1 to DV
      screen text '' at tx,det.y + r width tw
   next r
   lines = ''
   begin case
      case view = 1
         lines<-1> = 'API ON: SD listens on port 4247 and the firewall rule lets other computers on the network connect. LOCAL: SD listens on port 4247 and only this computer may connect. OFF: SD opens no API socket at all.'
         lines<-1> = 'SD opens or closes the API socket only when it starts, so a change to or from OFF asks whether to restart SD now, and a restart ends every session, this one too. A gives the terminal to REMOTE.API for that question.'
         lines<-1> = 'ssh ON lets other computers on the network connect over ssh; OFF lets only this computer connect, and ssh to this machine itself keeps working. It scopes the firewall rule and never stops or removes the ssh server.'
         lines<-1> = 'What is shown above is what the machine says, read back from sd.conf and the firewall rules, not what this page meant. Turning a door ON lets other computers reach this one, so its box wants the word OPEN typed.'
      case view = 2
         lines<-1> = 'A user account is reached by a door only if its Windows user is in the Windows group of that door: sdssh for ssh, sdapi for the whole API, sdfiles for the files-only route (sdfileswrite and sdfilesadmin add what it may do).'
         lines<-1> = 'When sdapi and sdfiles are both held, the API wins. NET is the register switch that lets the account open a file on another SD server. The switches are changed on TOOL.GATES (or modify.account), not here.'
         if nrows > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nu then lines<-1> = 'Under the cursor: ' : unames<ci> : ' - ' : ugates<ci>
      case view = 3
         lines<-1> = 'The servers are in the SDNet servers file of the system directory: a name, an address, the remote account and mode, the SHA-256 hash of the public key of the server (the pin) and the local accounts allowed to use it.'
         lines<-1> = 'A local account also needs the NET gate. X deletes the definition under the cursor (it does not ask itself; the box here does). N asks the fields, checks them, and gives the terminal to SET.SERVER.'
         if nsrv > 0 and ci >= 1 and ci <= nsrv then
            d = defs<ci>
            lines<-1> = ''
            lines<-1> = 'Under the cursor: ' : d<1, 1> : ' at ' : d<1, 2> : ':' : d<1, 3> : ', remote account ' : d<1, 4> : ', ' : d<1, 6> : ', defined ' : d<1, 8>
            lines<-1> = 'Full pin: ' : d<1, 5>
            lines<-1> = 'Local accounts that may use it: ' : (if d<1, 7> = '' then 'none' else d<1, 7>)
         end
      case view = 4
         lines<-1> = 'Every session now, with the kind it is: user (a terminal, the console or ssh), api (an API login, including the files-only route), sdnet (an SDNet client) and phantom. Where it came from is the address or terminal.'
         k.user = 0 ; k.api = 0 ; k.sdnet = 0 ; k.ph = 0
         for k = 1 to nsess
            fl = udata<k, 4>
            begin case
               case bitand(fl, USR$SDNET)
                  k.sdnet += 1
               case bitand(fl, USR$SDVBSRVR)
                  k.api += 1
               case bitand(fl, USR$PHANTOM)
                  k.ph += 1
               case 1
                  k.user += 1
            end case
         next k
         lines<-1> = k.user : ' user, ' : k.api : ' api, ' : k.sdnet : ' sdnet, ' : k.ph : ' phantom.'
      case 1
         lines<-1> = 'The certificate the API presents, and the hash of its public key: that hash is what another SD server pins in its definition of this machine (SET.SERVER ... pin).'
         lines<-1> = 'Give the public-key hash to the administrator of the other machine by a way you trust. The certificate fingerprint changes when it is renewed; the public-key hash does not.'
   end case
   n = 0
   for i = 1 to dcount(lines, @fm)
      call $tk_wrap(lines<i>, tw, pieces)
      for q = 1 to dcount(pieces, @fm)
         n += 1
         if n <= DV then
            pl = pieces<q>
            screen text pl[1, tw] at tx,det.y + n width tw
         end
      next q
   next i
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- keys and mouse

on.key:
   msg = ''
   if len(nm) = 1 and nm >= 'A' and nm <= 'Z' then nm = downcase(nm)
   begin case
      case nm = 'up'
         if ci > 1 then ci -= 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'down'
         if ci < nrows then ci += 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgup'
         ci -= VR
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'pgdn'
         ci += VR
         if ci > nrows then ci = nrows
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'home'
         ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm = 'end'
         ci = nrows
         if ci < 1 then ci = 1
         gosub redraw
      case nm >= '1' and nm <= '5' and len(nm) = 1
         view = nm + 0
         ci = 1 ; ta = 0
         gosub build.rows
         gosub draw.all
      case nm = 'a' and view = 1
         gosub do.api
      case nm = 's' and view = 1
         gosub do.ssh
      case nm = 'x' and view = 3
         gosub do.delete
      case nm = 'n' and view = 3
         gosub do.new
      case nm = 'ctrl-t'                    ;* S.179: the theme, kept for the person - the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('theme', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         if std.r<1> then gosub draw.all
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'act:std.mouse'             ;* S.186: View > Mouse, the same on every page ($tk_std)
         call $tk_std('mouse', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
         msg = std.r<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-o'                    ;* S.186: the log of the commands this page ran (View > Output; $tk_std)
         call $tk_std('output', ctx, keys, '', std.r)
      case nm = 'ctrl-k'                    ;* S.179: the keys of this page, in a box
         call $tk_std('keylist', ctx, keys, panes<view>, std.r)
      case nm = 'f5'
         gosub read.all
         gosub draw.all
         msg = 'read again'
      case nm = 'f1' or nm = '?'
         call $tk_help('box', 'tool.remote.page', hm, 0, 0)
         if hm # '' then msg = hm
      case nm = 'f6' or nm = 'shift-f6' or nm = 'act:ai'
         call $tk_aipage('ring', ctx, keys, 1, nm : @fm : 1, ap)            ;* S.176: F6 / Shift-F6 go round the boxes (one here: the view shown) and the AI line; AI > Ask the AI goes to the line
         msg = ap<2>
      case nm = 'ctrl-q'
         done = 1
      case nm = 'esc'
         if view # 1 then
            view = 1
            ci = 1 ; ta = 0
            gosub build.rows
            gosub draw.all
         end
   end case
   return

on.mouse:
   screen mouse returning mev else mev = ''
   if mev = '' then return
   mr = ''
   call $tk_menubar('click', ctx, keys, panes<view>, mev, '', mr)                 ;* a click on the bar on row 0
   if mr<1> # '' then
      nm = mr<4>
      if nm # '' then gosub on.key                          ;* a bar left with nothing chosen has no name: the status message stays
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('mouse', ctx, keys, panes<view>, mev, ap)                        ;* S.97 stage 2: a click on the AI line gives it the focus
   if ap # '' then
      msg = ap
      return
   end
   call $tk_help('hit', mev, mk.x, mk.y, hit.m)
   if hit.m then
      call $tk_help('box', 'tool.remote.page', hm, 0, 0)
      if hm # '' then msg = hm
      return
   end
   if mev<1> = 'press' and mev<2> = 1 then
      mx = mev<3>
      my = mev<4>
      if mx >= tx and mx <= tx + tw - 1 and my >= lst.y + 2 and my <= lst.y + 1 + VR then
         if ta + my - (lst.y + 1) <= nrows then
            ci = ta + my - (lst.y + 1)
            gosub redraw
         end
      end
   end
   return

* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the commands

* Is word a safe single word for the routine (a-z, 0-9, dot, dash, underscore, 1 to 32 characters)?  plain is 1 or 0
plain.word:
   plain = (word # '' and len(word) <= 32)
   for pi = 1 to len(word)
      if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789.-_', word[pi, 1], 1) = 0 then plain = 0
   next pi
   return

* sent and el are the sentence and its explanation, typed is null or the word to type; the box is shown, the command run when Run was chosen, everything read again, and the verb's words shown
confirm.and.run:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res = 'run' then
      call $tk_run(allow, sent, out, stat, err)
      gosub read.all
      gosub draw.all
      if err # '' then
         msg = err
      end else
         msg = sent[1, 60] : ' ran (status ' : stat : ')'
         lastl = ''
         for k = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
            if trim(out<k>) # '' then lastl = trim(out<k>)
         next k
         if lastl # '' then msg = msg : ': ' : lastl
      end
   end else
      msg = cmsg
   end
   return

* The same box, then the terminal is given to the verb (SET.SERVER's CONNECT step shows a key and asks whether to trust it) and the screen is taken again after it
confirm.and.hand.over:
   call $tk_confirm(sent, el, typed, res, cmsg)
   if res # 'run' then
      msg = cmsg
      return
   end
   call $tk_close(ctx)
   execute sent
   crt
   crt sysmsg(12870) :                                         ;* Press Enter to return
   input junk
   if junk = char(1) then null                                 ;* any answer goes back; the answer itself is not used
   call $tk_open('tool.remote', 'admin', ctx, err)
   if err # '' then
      display err
      done = 1
      return
   end
   call $tk_aipage('again', ctx, keys, '', '', aout)            ;* S.97 stage 2: the new context has no AI line yet
   gosub lay.declare                                           ;* the new context holds no panes; the window may be another size
   gen += 1
   ctx<TK.C.GEN> = gen
   gosub read.all
   gosub draw.all
   msg = 'back from ' : sent[1, 40] : ': the list shows what is defined now'
   return

* A: the API door
do.api:
   screen ask 'REMOTE.API: on, local or off' width 8 value '' title 'The API door' returning aw else return
   aw = downcase(trim(aw))
   if aw # 'on' and aw # 'local' and aw # 'off' then
      msg = 'the API door is on, local or off'
      return
   end
   sent = 'remote.api ' : aw
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   begin case
      case aw = 'on'
         typed = 'OPEN'
         el<-1> = 'SD listens on port 4247 and the firewall rule is opened for it: other computers on the network may connect to the API of this machine.'
      case aw = 'local'
         el<-1> = 'SD listens on port 4247 and the firewall rule lets only this computer connect.'
      case 1
         el<-1> = 'SD opens no API socket at all.'
   end case
   el<-1> = 'The terminal is given to REMOTE.API. SD opens or closes the socket only when it starts, so when the listener moves to or from OFF the verb asks whether to restart SD now (Enter answers no).'
   el<-1> = 'A restart ends every session, this one too; answered no, the change waits for the next start of SD. The firewall part takes effect at once.'
   gosub confirm.and.hand.over
   return

* S: the ssh door
do.ssh:
   screen ask 'REMOTE.SSH: on or off' width 8 value '' title 'The ssh door' returning sw else return
   sw = downcase(trim(sw))
   if sw # 'on' and sw # 'off' then
      msg = 'the ssh door is on or off'
      return
   end
   sent = 'remote.ssh ' : sw
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   if sw = 'on' then
      typed = 'OPEN'
      el<-1> = 'The firewall rule for the ssh server lets other computers on the network connect to this one over ssh.'
   end else
      el<-1> = 'The firewall rule for the ssh server lets only this computer connect over ssh; ssh to this machine itself keeps working.'
   end
   el<-1> = 'This scopes the firewall rule and never stops or removes the ssh server (SSH.SERVER REMOVE does that). Where there is no ssh server the verb refuses and says so. It takes effect at once.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* X: forget the server under the cursor
do.delete:
   if nsrv = 0 or ci < 1 or ci > nsrv then
      msg = 'there is no server to delete'
      return
   end
   d = defs<ci>
   word = d<1, 1>
   gosub plain.word
   if not(plain) then
      msg = 'this server name has characters this page will not put in a command; use delete.server at the prompt'
      return
   end
   sent = 'delete.server ' : word
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The definition of ' : word : ' (' : d<1, 2> : ':' : d<1, 3> : ') is removed from the servers file. No account can open its files after this.'
   el<-1> = 'The verb does not ask; this box is the question. set.server makes the definition again, but its pin must be typed or confirmed again.'
   gosub confirm.and.run
   return

* N: ask for the fields, check every one the way SET.SERVER does, then give the terminal to the verb
do.new:
   * S.88: one form with the seven answers in view; the first one SET.SERVER would refuse is said under the entries and the form stays
   spec = 'Define a server' : @fm : '&Define' : @fm : 'Pin: connect or 64 hex digits.  Port 4247 SD Core, 4249 Solo.'
   spec<-1> = 'name' : @vm : 'Name (a-z, 0-9)' : @vm : 18 : @vm : 16
   spec<-1> = 'host' : @vm : 'Host (DNS, IPv4, IPv6)' : @vm : 60 : @vm : 253
   spec<-1> = 'port' : @vm : 'API port' : @vm : 8 : @vm : 5
   spec<-1> = 'acc' : @vm : 'Account on the server' : @vm : 34 : @vm : 32
   spec<-1> = 'pin' : @vm : 'Pin' : @vm : 66 : @vm : 64
   spec<-1> = 'mode' : @vm : 'Files: read or write' : @vm : 8 : @vm : 8
   spec<-1> = 'accts' : @vm : 'Local accounts (a,b)' : @vm : 60 : @vm : 300
   fv = '' : @fm : '' : @fm : '4247' : @fm : '' : @fm : 'connect' : @fm : 'read' : @fm : ''
   call $tk_form('open', ctx, spec, fv, fo)
   if fo = 'no' then
      msg = 'the form does not fit this window: nothing was defined'
      return
   end
   loop
      call $tk_form('run', ctx, fans, fv, fid)
      if fans # 'ok' then
         call $tk_form('close', ctx, '', '', '')
         return
      end
      s.name = downcase(trim(fv<1>))
      s.host = downcase(trim(fv<2>))
      s.port = trim(fv<3>)
      s.acc = trim(fv<4>)
      s.pin = downcase(trim(fv<5>))
      s.mode = downcase(trim(fv<6>))
      s.accts = downcase(trim(fv<7>))
      fbad = '' ; fid = ''
      ok = (s.name # '' and len(s.name) <= 16 and s.name[1, 1] >= 'a' and s.name[1, 1] <= 'z')
      for q = 1 to len(s.name)
         if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', s.name[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
      next q
      if not(ok) then
         fbad = 'a server name is a lower case letter and up to 15 lower case letters or digits' ; fid = 'name'
      end
      if fbad = '' then
         ok = (s.host # '' and len(s.host) <= 253 and s.host[1, 1] # '-' and s.host[1, 1] # '.')
         for q = 1 to len(s.host)
            if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789.-:', s.host[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
         next q
         if not(ok) then
            fbad = 'a host is letters, digits, dots, hyphens and colons, not starting with a hyphen or a dot' ; fid = 'host'
         end
      end
      if fbad = '' then
         ok = (s.port # '' and len(s.port) <= 5)
         for q = 1 to len(s.port)
            if index('0123456789', s.port[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
         next q
         if ok then
            if (s.port + 0) < 1 or (s.port + 0) > 65535 then ok = 0
         end
         if not(ok) then
            fbad = 'a port is a number from 1 to 65535' ; fid = 'port'
         end
      end
      if fbad = '' then
         ok = (s.acc # '' and len(s.acc) <= 32)
         for q = 1 to len(s.acc)
            if index('abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789._-', s.acc[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
         next q
         if not(ok) then
            fbad = 'a remote account is up to 32 letters, digits, dots, underscores and hyphens' ; fid = 'acc'
         end
      end
      if fbad = '' then
         ok = (s.pin = 'connect')
         if not(ok) and len(s.pin) = 64 then
            ok = 1
            for q = 1 to 64
               if index('0123456789abcdef', s.pin[q, 1], 1) = 0 then ok = 0
            next q
         end
         if not(ok) then
            fbad = 'a pin is the word connect or exactly 64 hexadecimal digits' ; fid = 'pin'
         end
      end
      if fbad = '' and s.mode # 'read' and s.mode # 'write' then
         fbad = 'the mode is read or write' ; fid = 'mode'
      end
      if fbad = '' then
         ok = 1
         for w = 1 to dcount(s.accts, ',')
            wd = field(s.accts, ',', w)
            if s.accts # '' then
               if index(@fm : unames : @fm, @fm : wd : @fm, 1) = 0 then ok = 0
            end
         next w
         if not(ok) then
            fbad = 'each local account must be a registered USER account (see the routes view), separated by commas with no space' ; fid = 'accts'
         end
      end
      if fbad = '' then exit
      call $tk_form('say', ctx, fbad, fid, '')
   repeat
   call $tk_form('close', ctx, '', '', '')
   sent = 'set.server ' : s.name : ' ' : s.host : ' ' : s.port : ' ' : s.acc : ' ' : s.pin : ' ' : s.mode
   if s.accts # '' then sent := ' accounts ' : s.accts
   typed = ''
   el = ''
   el<-1> = 'The server ' : s.name : ' at ' : s.host : ':' : s.port : ' is defined, entered as account ' : s.acc : ', ' : s.mode : '. An existing definition of that name is replaced after the verb asks.'
   if s.pin = 'connect' then
      el<-1> = 'The terminal is given to the verb: it makes one TLS handshake, shows the key the server presents and the hash of it, and asks whether to trust it. Nothing is sent to the server.'
   end else
      el<-1> = 'The pin is the one you typed; nothing is dialled.'
   end
   el<-1> = 'The accounts that may use it also need the NET gate (modify.account name net-on).'
   gosub confirm.and.hand.over
   return

end

